{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 sets two gates and this trace fails both. The governing measurement is gps_trace.trace_distance_km, 12.51 km — the trip_record's 12.5 km is a rounded convenience copy that POL-RD-01 expressly forbids citing for the threshold test. Against the booked optimal of 11.8 km the excess is 0.71 km, which is 6.02% of optimal. Establishment requires an excess greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km absolute. 0.71 km is short of 0.8 km and 6.02% is short of 20%. POL-RD-01 is explicit that if either test fails no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The platform's own derived status for the trace is 'no deviation'.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02805", "EV-TRIP-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider filed and carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08: she must show an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, cited to evidence IDs. Limb (a) is satisfied — trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown all carry TRP-02805 and describe one trip. Limb (b) is not: her own claim measures 12.51 km against 11.8 km, the very same 0.71 km of excess the trace records, and that figure clears neither gate. The burden therefore never shifts to the driver and no exculpatory clause needs to be invoked on his behalf.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02805", "EV-TRIP-02805", "EV-FARE-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace the rider must rely on is clean, so the measurement cannot be attacked as a data failure and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises: 99 fixes at a 10-second sampling interval, 100.0% coverage, zero recorded gaps and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds. None of the POL-RD-07(a) to (c) impairment limbs is met, so the trace is not impaired for policy purposes, carries weight 1.0 and supplies the deciding fact at full confidence under POL-GEN-02. A claim cannot be escalated into money on this record; it has to be met on the numbers, and the numbers fail it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's contested SGD 2.00 has no counterpart anywhere in the policy arithmetic. The excess the trace records is 0.71 km, which at the fare card's 0.75 per km distance rate is 0.53 SGD of distance; the ledger confirms per_km_rate_sgd of 0.75 and distance_charged_km of 12.5. Even if the POL-RD-02 recomputation were run, it produces recomputed_fare of 17.9020 against charged_total of 18.54, a refund of 0.65 — below the rider's own figure. POL-RD-02 does not run at all here, because it opens only where a deviation is established under POL-RD-01, and none is.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02805", "EV-GPS-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The ledger is complete and reconciles: charged_total 18.54 SGD, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00 and 0.00 of ERP. On this rider-filed dispute, NO_ACTION under POL-GEN-03 leaves the present payment state as it stands — the charge remains in place and nothing is returned to the rider. The fare model is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 (upfront-quoted fares) has nothing to operate on, and the only refund route in this category, the POL-RD-02 recomputation, is closed by the threshold failure.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.payment_status",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing-integrity defect for the rider to collect on. No ERP gantry is charged — erp_gantries is empty and tolls_erp is 0.00 — and no airport surcharge is charged, airport_surcharge being 0.00 on a trip whose booked endpoints are Blk 231 Serangoon Ave 3 and Blk 456 Hougang Ave 10. The remaining lines are ordinary card amounts: base fare 3.80, distance 9.38, time 4.56, platform fee 0.80, no promo and no waiting-time fee. POL-RD-09(4) is available whether or not a deviation exists, but there is no unmatched or phantom line here for it to correct, so it yields the rider nothing.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-02805", "EV-TRIP-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Nothing on this record corroborates any finding against the driver. The chat log carries zero messages, so there is no admission of a detour and no chat corroboration of the kind POL-RD-07(ii) names; the fare ledger carries no unmatched gantry; and the driver's only statement, 'I followed the navigation' on the dispute record, is contradicted by no artifact — the trace is a single continuous 99-fix run with no gaps. No party asserts an external traffic cause here, and under POL-RD-13 an assertion that names no advisory artifact cannot be invoked against one, so there is no POL-RD-10(5) trigger and this case is decided on the threshold rather than sent to a human reviewer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-02805", "EV-FARE-02805", "EV-GPS-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-RD-13"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-06's profile check is not even engaged: materiality requires an excess above 50% of optimal or 8.0 km absolute, and the excess here is 6.02% and 0.71 km. Were it consulted it would find nothing — driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 172, so no pattern is established on the only field paths POL-RD-06 permits. No balanced-evidence resolution in the rider's favour, no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral is available to her, and POL-GEN-01 confines the profile to that single test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-02805", "EV-GPS-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own profile closes her last avenue: rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d is 0 and deviation_claims_60d_substantiated is 0, so the low-excess extra-corroboration condition in POL-RD-08 does not engage and nothing on her profile assists her either. The claim therefore stands or falls on the trace alone, and the trace gives 0.71 km of excess — below both POL-RD-01 gates. It falls.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-02805", "EV-GPS-02805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08", "POL-RD-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Outcome: the fare stands. The rider's dispute of SGD 2.00 is not supported by the evidence, so the SGD 18.54 already charged is left in place. No refund is issued to the rider and no compensation is paid to the driver.\n\nWhy. POL-RD-01 measures a deviation on the GPS trace, 12.51 km, which is the governing figure — the 12.5 km on the trip record is a rounded convenience copy and may not be cited for the threshold test — against the booked optimal route of 11.8 km. The excess is 0.71 km, or 6.02% of the optimal route. A deviation is established only if the excess is BOTH more than 20% of the optimal route (2.36 km on these figures) AND more than 0.8 km in absolute terms. It is neither. No deviation therefore exists on this trip and POL-RD-01 directs NO_ACTION however the trip felt to the rider. Because no deviation is established, POL-RD-02 never runs: for transparency only, run against the booked optimal it would have produced a recomputed fare of 17.9020 against the charged total of 18.54, i.e. 0.65, and the ruling must not move that money.\n\nThe trace is sound: 99 fixes at a 10-second interval against an expected 10 s, 100.0% coverage, an empty gaps list and max gap 0.0 s, admissibility COMPLETE at weight_multiplier 1.0. None of the POL-RD-07(a) to (c) impairment limbs is met, so there is no data failure, no discount under POL-GEN-02, and no trace-integrity escalation under POL-RD-07 / POL-RD-10(3). The measurement has to be met on its numbers, and the numbers are those both sides cite.\n\nNothing else in the bundle moves money. The fare ledger is complete and reconciles (base 3.80 + distance 9.38 + time 4.56 + platform fee 0.80 = 18.54 charged), with no ERP gantries, no tolls and no airport surcharge, so there is no phantom or unmatched line and POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to correct. The chat log contains 0 messages, so no rider-requested detour can be made out under POL-RD-04; neither pickup_amended_at nor dropoff_amended_at is set and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 cannot re-base the optimal route; and the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, so POL-RD-12 supplies no matched-itinerary baseline. No traffic advisory covers this trip — EV-ADVIS-02805-01 is MISSING at weight_multiplier 0.0 — so no closure or other external traffic cause can exonerate any part of the route, and no party in fact asserted one; the driver's answer, 'I followed the navigation', cites no artifact and under POL-RD-08 an assertion that cites no evidence carries no weight. That point is not decisive either way here, because the rider's own measured excess never clears the gate and the burden never shifted to the driver. The trip identifiers and timestamps on the trip record, the trace and the fare ledger agree, so no POL-RD-10(4) conflict arises, and every charge line has a counterpart in the trace or the trip record, so POL-RD-10(8) does not fire.\n\nThe profile claims were considered and decide nothing. POL-RD-06's pattern check is not engaged — there is no material deviation (6.02% and 0.71 km against the 50% / 8.0 km materiality gates) and the evidence is not finely balanced — and it would in any case find nothing, since driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 172 completed trips in 90 days. There is accordingly no FULL_REFUND uplift and no POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral, which is why the referrals list is empty. The rider's rider_profile.deviation_claims_60d of 0 means the extra-corroboration condition in POL-RD-08 is not engaged. All other profile fields mentioned on either side are CONTEXT ONLY under POL-GEN-01 and none was used as a ground of decision.\n\nConfidence is 0.90. The deciding measurement is carried by the GPS trace and the trip record, both at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the cap is 1.0 and the ruling is well above the 0.70 escalation floor. The monetary effect is nil and so is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold. This is a provisional ruling made without human review; either party may appeal it once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: the complaint is that the trip ran 12.51 km against a usual-route distance of 11.8 km. Both figures are on the record — 12.51 km is gps_trace.trace_distance_km on EV-GPS-02805 and 11.8 km is trip_record.optimal_distance_km on EV-TRIP-02805 — and the platform's own derived excess is 0.71 km, or 6.02% of the optimal route. POL-RD-01 establishes a route deviation only when the excess is BOTH more than 0.8 km in absolute terms AND more than 20% of the optimal distance. 0.71 km is short of 0.8 km, and 6.02% is short of 20%. Both tests must pass, so no deviation is established on this trip and the outcome is NO_ACTION: charged_total of SGD 18.54 stands and nothing is returned. Because the gate fails, the POL-RD-02 recomputation never opens; the driver's arithmetic (charged_total 18.54 less a recomputed_fare of 17.9020, i.e. SGD 0.65) is correct as far as it goes but cannot ground an award, and equally no line of the fare ledger supports the SGD 2.00 the rider contests. The rider's measured excess is confirmed by the same telemetry the rider cites, so the finding is not a credibility finding against either party — the trace simply does not clear the threshold. On evidence quality: EV-GPS-02805 carries 99 fixes at a 10-second interval, 100.0% coverage, an empty gaps list and a maximum gap of 0.0 seconds, all at weight 1.0, so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) and no POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises; EV-TRIP-02805 and EV-FARE-02805 are likewise at weight 1.0, and the identifiers and timestamps on all three agree. The bundle holds no traffic advisory — EV-ADVIS-02805-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 with issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — and that absence is itself citable, but it changes nothing: no party invoked a road-closure exoneration under POL-RD-03, so there is nothing for the absence to defeat, and under POL-RD-13 a missing advisory does not escalate a case decided on the threshold. The driver's answer, 'I followed the navigation', cites no artifact and carries no weight; it is also moot, since the measurement itself shows no deviation. EV-CHAT-02805 contains 0 messages, so there is no rider-requested detour under POL-RD-04 and no driver admission; vehicle_type is RYDE_X and no endpoint was amended, so POL-RD-05 and POL-RD-12 have nothing to re-base. No ERP gantry and no airport surcharge were charged and the ledger reconciles, so POL-RD-09(4) yields the rider nothing and no billing-integrity referral is produced. No driver compensation arises either: the fare billed 12.5 km against a trace of 12.51 km, a shortfall of 0.01 km, far below the 1.0 km POL-RD-04 requires. POL-RD-06 is not engaged (the excess is neither 50% of optimal nor 8.0 km, so there is no material deviation and no finely balanced evidence), and in any event driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 172 completed trips in 90 days, so no pattern exists; the rider's deviation_claims_60d is 0, so POL-RD-08's extra-corroboration condition does not apply. The profile fields both sides mention are context only under POL-GEN-01 and carried nothing in this ruling. No POL-RD-10 trigger fired, so there is no escalation; the monetary effect is zero and therefore below the execution threshold, so nothing is held and nothing executes."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
